#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0018 expect=noViolation domain=ADLBC
#note "PMDA AD0018: the column is literally named CRITy (lower-case y) and its dataset label differs from the Library label, so only the wildcard-index carve-out can keep the rule silent. Premise changed 2026-09-28 (owner: these rules check case insensitive): the leaf is var_name(\"LIBRARY\") !~ /[a-z]/ - the engine's OWN template predicate (WildcardExpander: a name is a wildcard if it starts with '*' or contains any lower-case letter) applied to the LIBRARY name the column resolved to - so CRITy is recognised as the template CRITy and nothing fires; the data's own case no longer decides it. Pins the live carve-out (Fix #282, ruling M2-D15). The previous leaf /(?:^|[^A-Z])(?:y|zz|xx|w)(?:[^A-Z]|$)/ required the marker to follow a non-upper-case character and matched 0 of 143 real ADaM template names, so this fired once at variable_name=CRITy."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
#library variable-metadata ADLBC CRITy name=CRITy label="Analysis Criterion y"
#expectViolationCount 0
dataset ADLBC structure=BDS
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col PARAMCD type=Char label="Parameter Code"
col CRITy   type=Char label="Wrong Label"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALT | AGE-GT-60
